# samples/real.list.example — TEMPLATE. Every entry below is INVENTED.
#
# Copy it to samples/real.list (which is gitignored) and put your own material
# in it. Nothing of yours belongs in this file: it is committed, the repo is
# public, and a bundle slug is made of the first words you actually said.
#
#   cp samples/real.list.example samples/real.list
#   $EDITOR samples/real.list          # ls drafts/ and sync/Obsidian/ for names
#   bin/arm.sh samples                 # builds samples/real/ (also gitignored)
#
# Two columns, tab-separated: `memo` names a directory in drafts/, `note` names
# a file in sync/Obsidian/ (without the .md).
#
# Pick for CONVERGENCE, not for quality. A test corpus is only useful if there
# is genuinely something in it to find, so choose material that circles the same
# problem from more than one direction — ideally some dictated and some typed,
# since that pairing is what the curator is hunting for. Two or three clusters
# of three or four pieces each is plenty; include one long recording if you want
# long posts exercised.
#
# --- everything below is lorem ipsum, and is meant to be replaced ------------
